<!-- ============ AT THE COUNTER ============ -->
<section class="ac-royal sunk section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">At the Counter</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Four ways to get a customer on the record.</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">None of them slow the queue, and none rely on an associate typing an email address correctly. All four land in the same record.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="captx" role="img" aria-label="Four capture routes all converging on one customer record.">
      <div class="captx-routes">
        <div class="captx-route">
          <span class="captx-n">01</span>
          <div class="captx-body"><strong>Associate-entered</strong><p>Customizable quick fields for a fast capture, or a full-page form when there is time to take everything.</p></div>
          <span class="captx-arrow"><i class="ti ti-arrow-right"></i></span>
        </div>
        <div class="captx-route">
          <span class="captx-n">02</span>
          <div class="captx-body"><strong>Customer-facing mode</strong><p>The app switches into a secure customer-facing state and hands the device over for the shopper to register themselves.</p></div>
          <span class="captx-arrow"><i class="ti ti-arrow-right"></i></span>
        </div>
        <div class="captx-route">
          <span class="captx-n">03</span>
          <div class="captx-body"><strong>QR self-registration</strong><p>A printed or on-screen QR opens a self-fill page on the shopper's own phone. On submit, the record is captured and tied to that exact store location, then "show recent" attaches it to the open ticket instantly.</p></div>
          <span class="captx-arrow"><i class="ti ti-arrow-right"></i></span>
        </div>
        <div class="captx-route">
          <span class="captx-n">04</span>
          <div class="captx-body"><strong>Wallet & membership scan</strong><p>Pull an existing account onto the checkout screen by scanning a loyalty membership QR or digital wallet ID with the device camera.</p></div>
          <span class="captx-arrow"><i class="ti ti-arrow-right"></i></span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="captx-target">
        <span class="captx-target-ring"></span>
        <i class="ti ti-user-heart"></i>
        <strong>One customer record</strong>
        <span>Cleansed, deduplicated, per market</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mini-grid mini-grid-2" style="margin-top: 40px;">
        <div class="mini-card"><h3>Profile depth</h3><p>Membership status, custom preferences, birthday tracking, appointments, lifetime spend indicators, and the full transaction log, surfaced where the associate is standing.</p></div>
        <div class="mini-card"><h3>Omnichannel wish lists</h3><p>Wish lists update in real time whether they were edited online or in the store, so the list on screen is the list the customer is looking at.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
<section class="ac-blue section" style="padding-bottom: 80px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Customer data questions, answered.</h2>
    </div>
    <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Is this a CDP, and how does it sit alongside our CRM?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>It performs the role a customer data platform plays for store retail: unified customer profiles holding preferences, purchase history, and engagement data, captured through self-registration and tied to transactions at the point of sale. It is designed to sit alongside your existing CRM rather than replace it. Open customer APIs import and export customer information, so you keep the CRM workflows you already run.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          How does customer sign-up work at the register?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Customers register themselves by scanning a QR code on their own device, so nobody types details at the cash wrap and the queue keeps moving. A scannable barcode ties the new profile to the transaction and receipt instantly, and email or SMS marketing consent is captured during registration.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Does this replace our CRM?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>No. Open customer APIs import and export customer information, so it supports the CRM workflows you already run rather than requiring a full migration. Records are cleansed and deduplicated, with languages, locations, and registration templates configured per market.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          What is 121 Commerce?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>121 Commerce is where customer intelligence and product intelligence converge at the point of sale: real-time associate guidance backed by the customer's history and the live product record. AI customer sessions capture what was asked and recommended, enabling continuous AI improvement and customer insight. </p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-question" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('open')">
          Can we collect post-purchase feedback?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Dynamic QR codes generated on receipts invite customers into a survey after they buy, which turns a receipt into a feedback channel without a separate email campaign.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

